  "question": {
    "text": "Let P be a matrix of order <math><mn>3</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>3</mn></math> such that all the entries in P are from the set <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced close=\"}\" open=\"{\" separators=\"|\"><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>&#160;</mi><mn>0,</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced></math> . Then, the maximum possible value of the determinant of P is _______."
  },
  "options": [],
  "correct_answer": "4",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<math><mo>&#8710;</mo><mo>=</mo><mfenced close=\"|\" open=\"|\" separators=\"|\"><mrow><mtable><mtr><mtd><msub><mrow><mi>a</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mtd><mtd><msub><mrow><mi>a</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></mtd><mtd><msub><mrow><mi>a</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></msub></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msub><mrow><mi>b</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mtd><mtd><msub><mrow><mi>b</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></mtd><mtd><msub><mrow><mi>b</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></msub></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msub><mrow><mi>c</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mtd><mtd><msub><mrow><mi>c</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></mtd><mtd><msub><mrow><mi>c</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></msub></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mtable><mtr><mtd><munder accentunder=\"false\"><mrow><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><msub><mrow><mi>a</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><msub><mrow><mi>b</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><msub><mrow><mi>c</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mrow><mi>a</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><msub><mrow><mi>b</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></msub><msub><mrow><mi>c</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mrow><mi>a</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></msub><msub><mrow><mi>b</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><msub><mrow><mi>c</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mfenced></mrow><mo>&#9183;</mo></munder></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mi>x</mi></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>-</mo><mtable><mtr><mtd><munder accentunder=\"false\"><mrow><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><msub><mrow><mi>a</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></msub><msub><mrow><mi>b</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><msub><mrow><mi>c</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mrow><mi>a</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><msub><mrow><mi>b</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><msub><mrow><mi>c</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mrow><mi>a</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><msub><mrow><mi>b</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></msub><msub><mrow><mi>c</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mfenced></mrow><mo>&#9183;</mo></munder></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mi>y</mi></mtd></mtr></mtable></math><br />Now if <math><mi>x</mi><mo>&#8804;</mo><mn>3</mn></math> and <math><mi>y</mi><mo>&#8805;</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></math><br />The <math><mo>&#8710;</mo></math> can be maximum 6 but it is not possible<br />because&nbsp;<math><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>&#8658;</mo></math> each term of <math><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math><br />And <math><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>-3</mn><mo>&#8658;</mo></math> each term of <math><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></math><br /><math><mo>&#8658;</mo></math> <math><mrow><munderover><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#8719;</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></munderover><mrow><msub><mrow><mi>a</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><msub><mrow><mi>b</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><msub><mrow><mi>c</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mi>&#160;</mi></math> and <math><mrow><munderover><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#8719;</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></munderover><mrow><msub><mrow><mi>a</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><msub><mrow><mi>b</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><msub><mrow><mi>c</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></math>, which is a contradiction.<br />Now for value to be&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5</mn></math>&nbsp;one the terms must be zero but that will make two terms zero which means answer cannot be&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5</mn></math>. Next possibility is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn></math>&nbsp;which&nbsp;can be obtained as <math><mfenced close=\"|\" open=\"|\" separators=\"|\"><mrow><mtable><mtr><mtd><mn>1</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>1</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>1</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>1</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>1</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>1</mn></mtd><mtd><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>1</mn></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn></math>"
  }
